 "notes": [
  "tasks.jsonl holds exactly the 129 public instances (4 repos), so the design doc's 'exclude all 129' rule would empty the set. Operative law: the task-level 60/15/25 split (source.task_split), verified against split_map(load_tasks()); the paper must not present public-set numbers as private-set estimates.",
  "preserve_thinking=true is mandatory: with the default false the template's thinking_gate drops intermediate thoughts on tool-call turns, contradicting 'thinking tokens are learning targets'.",
  "Rows whose own `split` disagreed with source.task_split were re-split at the row level; the task boundary is the only boundary that carries.",
  "repo_share_realized counts synthetic rows under repo='synthetic'; they are bounded by the same per-repo cap as real repos, which is what keeps the share honest.",
  "unit cap key is (split, family, subtype, cap_key) where cap_key is the file path for real tasks, the graph seed for graph rows, and a hash of the generated spec for synthetic rows; it is written to every output row as `unit` so the cap is auditable."
 ],
